# Cómo citar el observatorio (Citation File Format). Los mismos créditos van dentro de cada fichero
# de datos publicado (configuracion/licencia_datos.json). / How to cite the observatory.
cff-version: 1.2.0
message: >-
  Si usas estos datos, cítalos así / If you use this data, please cite it as below:
  Alaniz Pintos, L. (2026). European Observatory of Drone Incidents. Versión / Version 2026-10.
  https://droneobservatory.eu. Licencia / Licence CC BY 4.0.
  Para un trabajo académico, cita la versión archivada con DOI / For academic work, cite the
  archived version with DOI (Discuss Data, one every quarter): see preferred-citation.
type: dataset
title: European Observatory of Drone Incidents
authors:
  - family-names: Alaniz Pintos
    given-names: Lucas
    name-suffix: PhD
    orcid: "https://orcid.org/0009-0008-5179-2534"
version: "2026-10"
date-released: "2026-10-01"
license: CC-BY-4.0
url: "https://droneobservatory.eu"
repository-code: "https://github.com/QuantuSync/droneobservatory"
repository-artifact: "https://droneobservatory.eu/datos/versiones/2026-10"
abstract: >-
  Public register of drone incidents in Europe, each with its sources and its level of
  confirmation, and of drone attacks on Ukraine according to official reports. The data
  (incidents, statuses, classifications and figures) are published under CC BY 4.0; the code is
  under Apache-2.0. Monthly citable versions: https://droneobservatory.eu/metodologia#versiones.
keywords:
  - EODI
  - drones
  - Europe
  - incidents
  - open data
identifiers:
  - type: doi
    value: 10.48320/F2CA4AE9-B2D3-4B0F-8F58-6CFBDE30D39F
    description: >-
      Version 1.0 (2026-11-02) archived in Discuss Data (Research Centre for East European
      Studies, University of Bremen), with copies in Zenodo and DARIAH: 383 incidents in 26
      countries, data published up to 2026-11-02T10:17Z. A new version, with its own DOI, is
      deposited every quarter (January, April, July and October).
  - type: url
    value: "https://discuss-data.net/dataset/f2ca4ae9-b2d3-4b0f-8f58-6cfbde30d39f/"
    description: Version 1.0 in Discuss Data.
  - type: url
    value: "https://droneobservatory.eu/metodologia#versiones"
    description: >-
      Monthly citable versions of the open data on the website, frozen on the 1st of each
      month with their SHA-256 fingerprints.
preferred-citation:
  type: data
  abbreviation: EODI
  title: >-
    European Observatory of Drone Incidents (EODI): drone incidents in Europe – Open register of
    drone incidents with sources, literal quotations and official status
  authors:
    - family-names: Alaniz Pintos
      given-names: Lucas
      orcid: "https://orcid.org/0009-0008-5179-2534"
  year: 2026
  date-released: "2026-11-02"
  version: "1.0"
  doi: 10.48320/F2CA4AE9-B2D3-4B0F-8F58-6CFBDE30D39F
  url: "https://doi.org/10.48320/F2CA4AE9-B2D3-4B0F-8F58-6CFBDE30D39F"
  repository: "https://discuss-data.net/dataset/f2ca4ae9-b2d3-4b0f-8f58-6cfbde30d39f/"
  publisher:
    name: Discuss Data
  license: CC-BY-4.0
  notes: >-
    Version 2026-11-02, v. 1.0. The measured air traffic file is under ODbL 1.0.
